=== CO5 TASK B2: SIMULATE UNDER VARYING CONDITIONS ===
  1. Baseline (50M, 20ms, 20 users)            | Thr= 5.54 Mbps | Voice Delay= 20.04 ms | Voice Loss= 0.0%
  2. Higher Load (50M, 20ms, 80 users)         | Thr=17.50 Mbps | Voice Delay= 20.07 ms | Voice Loss= 0.0%
  3. Tight Link + High Delay (20M, 80ms, 50u)  | Thr=11.50 Mbps | Voice Delay= 80.32 ms | Voice Loss= 0.0%
  4. + Background Download FIFO (20M, 20ms)    | Thr=20.41 Mbps | Voice Delay=101.61 ms | Voice Loss=39.0%
  5. + Background Download + Voice Priority    | Thr=20.58 Mbps | Voice Delay= 20.39 ms | Voice Loss=39.0%

Interpretation:
  - Adding a 24 Mbps background file download on a 20 Mbps FIFO link saturates the buffer,
    spiking voice delay and dropping packets (run 4).
  - Enabling strict Priority Queueing for voice (run 5) isolates voice delay right back near prop_ms with 0% loss!

--- Alternative Concept Analysis: Packet Tracer vs NS-3 ---
  - Packet Tracer: Visual GUI, real Cisco IOS CLI, minimal setup effort (~10 min), but simplified queue/TCP internals.
  - NS-3 (C++/Python): Packet-by-packet ns-3::QueueDisc, exact CUBIC/BBR & Wi-Fi PHY models, reproducible traces, higher coding effort.

